course: dictionary
lesson: 1850
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The words around it are the clues that show which meaning the writer means. Coco is a good example: it can mean a tree, a name, or part of a brand.
explain: «The coco de mer, a huge double nut from the Seychelles islands, was once found floating in the Indian Ocean.» The clues are nut, islands and floating. They tell you this coco is a tree and its nut, not a person.
explain: «Isn't that your sister's dress?» Coco twirls: «Yeah, it's vintage, babe.» The capital C and the twirling tell you Coco is a name for a person. Always ask: what does this sentence need here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Coco can mean the coconut palm, the tall tropical tree that grows coconuts.
fact: Coco is also short for coconut, as in «coco fibre» and «coco husk».
fact: Coco is a first name or pet name, like the fashion designer Coco Chanel or a pet dog called Coco.
fact: Coco is part of brand and film names, such as Coco Pops and the Disney film «Coco».
fact: A capital letter, as in «Coco», often shows that the word is a name.
exercise: «The coco de mer, a huge double nut from the Seychelles islands, was once found floating in the Indian Ocean.» In this sentence, coco means what? | A breakfast cereal | A pet dog | A person's first name | *A tree that grows coconuts
exercise: «Isn't that your sister's dress?» Coco twirls. In this sentence, what kind of word is Coco? | A coconut | A cereal | A plant-pot fibre | *A person's name
exercise: Which phrase shows coco as a short form of coconut? | *Coco fibre | Coco Chanel | Coco Pops | Coco the dog
test: The fashion designer Coco Chanel shows that Coco can be a | A coconut husk | A tree | *A first name | A breakfast cereal
test: In the phrase «coco palm», coco means | A fashion designer | A Disney film | *The coconut tree | A pet dog
exam: Read: «Coco twirls in her vintage dress.» Which best explains Coco? | A breakfast cereal | A tree on the beach | A coconut | *A girl's name, because the capital letter and the person twirling show it
